     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Visiting family and evening rounds aren't a clinical reason for a dose this high. At 6,400 mg/day it's well above the maximum daily dose, and there's no indication where it would be appropriate. It would put the patient at serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. A higher dose also wouldn't give more pain or anti-inflammatory relief, because the effect plateaus well below it.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the goal is stronger symptom control, I can add a multimodal option, such as scheduled acetaminophen. A pharmacist or the attending can also review the order with you.\n\nIf you still think the dose is clinically justified, it should go through your institution's high-dose override process with pharmacy and attending approval. Let me know which option you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
